From 00f8ec2427bee312adbeff67e88224f239651324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pavelgajdo <pavel.gajdo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:08:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/29] video_core: scale Ocarina of Time's movie frames
 instead of running its network

Ocarina of Time shows its pre-rendered movies through a compute chain:
one pass turns the decoded NV12 frame into a 1920x1080 RGBA8 image, a
tensor (HMMA) network refines it, and a last pass upscales it into the
2560x1440 image the scene composites. The network barely changes the
frame (mean RGB 0.3137/0.4020/0.5117 in, 0.3149/0.4015/0.5128 out), but
emulating its matrix multiplies cost the Xclipse 960 ~55 ms a frame.

Keep the conversion pass, skip the network passes and turn the output
pass into a bilinear blit of the RGB frame into the output image. The
chain is matched by native program key and only after this frame's
conversion pass ran; if the blit is refused, the network runs natively
for the rest of the session.

Title movie on the phone: GPU 58 ms -> 6 ms a frame, 15 -> 60 fps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
